{"id":"neet-2025-q040","pn":40,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Semiconductor Electronics","st":"Full wave rectifier","q":"A full wave rectifier circuit with diodes (D₁) and (D₂) is shown in the figure. If input supply voltage V_in = 220sin(100πt) volt, then at t = 15 msec","o":["D₁ is forward biased, D₂ is reverse biased","D₁ is reverse biased, D₂ is forward biased.","D₁ and D₂ both are forward biased","D₁ and D₂ both are reverse biased"],"c":1,"s":"V_in = 220sin(100πt) volt, t = 15 ms = 0.015 s.\nω = 100π, so 2π/T = 100π.\nT = 1/50 s = 0.02 s.\nSo t = 3T/4, i.e. the negative half cycle.\nThe negative half cycle makes D₁ reverse biased and D₂ forward biased.","fig":{"w":370,"h":215,"alt":"Full-wave rectifier: AC source and primary coil, transformer with centre-tapped secondary, diodes D1 and D2 joined to load RL and two output terminals","d":[["l",37,42,93,42],["l",37,42,37,94],["l",37,120,37,170],["l",37,170,93,170],["l",93,42,93,85],["p","M93 85 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 93 96.8 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 93 108.6 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 93 120.4 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 93 132.2"],["l",93,132,93,170],["c",37,107,13],["t",37,111,"~","m"],["t",5,111,"V"],["t",15,117,"in","s"],["l",110,78,110,122],["l",120,78,120,122],["p","M138 85 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 138 96.8 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 138 108.6 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 138 120.4 A5.9 5.9 0 0 0 138 132.2"],["l",138,85,138,42],["l",138,42,232,42],["l",138,132,138,170],["l",138,170,232,170],["p","M232 34 L232 50 L248 42 Z"],["l",250,34,250,50],["l",250,42,281,42],["p","M232 162 L232 178 L248 170 Z"],["l",250,162,250,178],["l",250,170,281,170],["l",281,42,281,170],["l",281,122,356,122],["c",360,122,4],["l",312,122,312,138],["p","M312 138 L307 141.7 L317 149 L307 156.3 L317 163.7 L307 171 L317 178.3 L312 182"],["l",312,182,312,205],["l",177,205,356,205],["c",360,205,4],["l",177,158,177,117],["l",177,117,162,117,"a"],["p","M177 158 A12 12 0 0 0 177 182"],["l",177,182,177,205],["t",249,28,"D"],["t",259,32,"1","s"],["t",245,150,"D"],["t",255,154,"2","s"],["t",325,168,"R"],["t",334,172,"L","s"]]}}
